@show daniel neutral at=c
@cam closeup daniel
> Daniel has gone quiet. Not the performing kind, where he holds his breath and his knee bounces. The other one. The one from the floor of the practice room.
> In Mr. Kim's corner there is only a dark cabinet and a rubber plant. The lobby ticks.
> He's looking at you. Not checking the score. Just looking, the way you'd look at the fourth frame.
daniel: You picked the booth.
you: I picked the booth.
daniel[smile]: Okay. I've got about two minutes of not knowing what to say. It's a record. Don't tell Charlie.
> Two minutes. It's enough time to say one true thing, and you find that you know which one.
* [romantic] Take his hand, here, in front of everyone. "I'm not leaving when it stops." {if daniel.romance >= 4}
    @goto daniel_ending
* [sincere] "Wherever you all end up after this — save me the seat beside you. Not across. Beside."
    @goto daniel_ending_beside
* [quiet] "There's something I want to tell you. I don't want to fit it into two minutes."
    @goto daniel_ending_someday

=== daniel_ending_beside
@bg studio_lobby t=fade
@music echo
@amb room
@fx memory n=0.8
@cam wide
> Beside. It's a small word. You watch it land on him like a blanket that smells of a cupboard.
@show daniel neutral at=c
daniel: …Not across.
you: Across is where the audience sits.
daniel[thinking]: Yeah. It is. I've been putting everyone I like across from me for years. So I could see if they were bored.
daniel[smile]: Beside's harder. You can't see their face. You just have to believe they're still there.
you: I'll still be there.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 08. Preserving. Eight frames. One margin note. One index word.
@textbox normal
@sfx chime
> The glass card slides out of the desk, warm as a cup. Eight tiny frames, and under them, in letters you need to tilt it to read, the word you chose in the archive.
@if var.danielx_label == "staying"
    > STAYING.
@elif var.danielx_label == "dry"
    > DRY.
@else
    > NOTHING, THE GOOD KIND.
@show charlie smile at=l
charlie: It's the booth. And there's a word on it. Do they all get a word, or only the ones somebody stopped to choose?
@show hanbi smile at=r
hanbi: Only those. Somebody sat on a cold floor for that one.
charlie[smile]: …Then it's the right word. You can tell.
@hide charlie
@hide hanbi
> Daniel holds one edge of the card and leaves you the other. He isn't grinning at it. He's smiling, which on him is the quieter instrument.
daniel: Thanks, ECHO. For all five. And for the forty seconds.
@textbox echo
echo: You are welcome, Recipient Daniel. Your file now reads: CAN SIT STILL. I did not think I would get to write that.
@textbox normal
@hide all
@call echo_farewell
@time 05:45
@bg dawn_cafe t=slow d=2.4
@music dawn
@amb cafe
@fx dust n=0.5
@cam reveal
> The breakfast place is four streets from the studio and has been open since five for taxi drivers. It has one long table, by the window, and this morning it has all of you.
@cg cg_daniel_x5
> You're last through the door. You stopped outside to look at the building once more from the pavement, because for once you wanted to see a place before you walked away from it, and not after.
> It's very loud in here. Hyunjun is ordering one more of something. Songha is writing the orders down in a notebook with one page missing. Hamin is counting who hasn't got water.
> Eight people, nine chairs.
> The ninth has an iridescent windbreaker thrown over the back of it, arms out, like it's holding off a crowd.
@show daniel smile at=c
daniel: {{playerName}}. Here. I've been holding this for ten minutes. Justin tried for it twice. I had to use the jacket.
> It's the chair next to his. Not the one facing him. He's turned his own a little, so that the two of them point the same way, out at the room.
> You sit. The plush is already on the table between your places, leaning on the napkin holder, like somebody who got here early.
@cg off
@show songha smile at=l
songha: For the record, I've put you both down for the soup. He said you'd want the soup. He was very sure.
daniel[smile]: I guessed. You looked like soup.
@hide songha
* [sincere] "You saved it."
    @rel daniel trust+1
    daniel[smile]: You asked me to. It's the first thing anyone's asked me for that wasn't a bit. I wasn't going to get it *wrong*.
* [playful] "Defended it from Justin. With a jacket. I'm moved."
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    daniel[laugh]: It was a siege. He's very persistent before he's eaten.
* [quiet] Put your half of the strip on the table, face up.
    @rel daniel trust+1
    > He looks at it. Then he unzips the zipped pocket, and puts his half down above yours, and nudges it with one finger until the torn edges meet.
@cam closeup daniel
> The table goes on being loud round you. Somebody's telling the mole story already. It has grown a second sofa.
> Daniel isn't adding to it. He's got his elbows on the table and his shoulder against yours, and he's just listening to his friends. You can feel that his knee is still.
daniel[neutral]: Can I tell you what I worked out? On the walk?
you: Tell me.
daniel: I've got seven people who'd do anything for me. I know that. And every one of them, I'd keep entertained till I fell over.
daniel: I've never had one I could be boring at. On purpose. Where that was the whole job.
daniel[smile]: I'm not dressing it up as anything else. I don't want it to be anything else. I want it to be this, for a really long time.
daniel: You're my person. The beside one. If that's a thing you'd want to be.
you: I've never been anyone's anything for long enough to have a seat.
you: I'd like to find out what it's like. I'd like it to be yours.
> He doesn't say anything. He puts his phone on the table between the soups and turns it so you can see.
> Your number, from the back of his half, or from ECHO, who never asked. He's typing the name. He deletes it twice.
> What he saves, in the end, is *FRAME FOUR*.
@if var.danielx_back == "plain"
    daniel[smile]: You said call when it's quiet. I'm going to. I'm going to ring you and say nothing, and you're going to say nothing back, and it's going to be the best part of my week.
@else
    daniel[smile]: I'm going to ring you when it's quiet, and not say anything. You don't have to either. We'll just have the line open. If that suits you.
you: I'll pick up.
daniel: Every time?
you: Every time. I'll be beside the phone.
daniel[laugh]: *Beside*. You're doing it on purpose now.
@show charlie thinking at=r
charlie: You two are the only quiet ones at the table. I'm checking, not prying. Everything all right?
daniel[smile]: Everything's all right. Nothing's happening. It's great. Eat your eggs.
charlie[smile]: …Good. It suits you both, whatever it is.
@hide charlie
> The soup comes. He pushes the better spoon across to you without looking, the way you'd do for someone you'd known for years.
> Outside the window the street goes from grey to peach, and a taxi driver at the counter asks for the radio on, and nobody at the long table notices the time.
> There's a chair with your coat on it now. On the way in you'd have called that a small thing.
> Daniel leans back, in a seat that faces the same way as yours, and for a whole minute he lets the morning go by without saying one word about it.
> You count it for him. You don't tell him how long.
@ending daniel_beside
@credits

=== daniel_ending_someday
@bg studio_lobby t=fade
@music echo
@amb room
@fx memory n=0.8
@cam wide
> He hears it. You watch him hear it: the thing, and the fact that you aren't going to hurry it.
@show daniel neutral at=c
daniel: …Is it a good thing? The thing you don't want to fit in?
you: It's a good thing.
daniel[smile]: Okay. Then don't fit it. I can wait two minutes. I've sat still for longer. I've got a certificate.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 08. Preserving. Eight frames. One margin note. One index word.
@textbox normal
@sfx chime
> The glass card slides out of the desk, warm as a cup. Eight tiny frames. He holds it up to the last of the Archive Wall, and then holds it lower, where you can see it too.
@show haruta smile at=l
haruta: It ends on the quiet frame. That's brave. Most people would cut before it.
@show hyunjun smile at=r
hyunjun: One more, all of us, if there's film. There's never film. I ask on principle.
@hide haruta
@hide hyunjun
daniel: Thanks, ECHO. For trying four hundred and twelve times.
@textbox echo
echo: You are welcome, Recipient Daniel. The rain won every time but the last. I have noted the last.
@textbox normal
@hide all
@call echo_farewell
@time 05:32
@bg dawn_rooftop t=slow d=2.4
@music dawn
@amb birds
@fx light n=0.5
@cam reveal
> The others are downstairs finding their shoes. Songha is doing a headcount. Hanbi is turning off the lights, because somebody should.
> You and Daniel have come back up to the roof. Nobody said why. There's one item open on a folded page, and this is where it happens.
> The lamp on its tripod is only a lamp. The blankets are where everyone left them. Over the laundromat the sky has gone the colour of the inside of a shell.
@show daniel neutral at=c
> He stands at the low wall with his hands on it. You stand next to him. It's cold enough to see your breath, and neither of you minds.
daniel: It's been more than two minutes.
you: It has.
> You've left a great many places without saying the one true thing about them. You're good at it. You'd like, this once, to be bad at it.
you: I like you, Daniel. Not the night. Not the booth. You, with the list, and you without it.
you: I've known since the radiator. I wanted to say it somewhere that wasn't about to be switched off.
> He doesn't pose. His hand doesn't even twitch. He just looks at you, steadily, while the colour comes up in his face like the sky behind him.
daniel[shy]: Me too. I like you. The larger word. The one that was under "calm."
daniel: I was going to say it on the stairs and I turned it into a joke about ECHO. I'm sorry. It was a good joke. This is better.
@cam closeup daniel
> And there it is, said, by both of you, in the open air, and nothing falls over.
> He laughs — the low one, the one that doesn't look round afterwards.
daniel[thinking]: Can I say the next part? Tell me if it's wrong.
daniel: I don't want to do it all now. At half five. On no sleep, in a cupboard blanket.
daniel: All night I've been learning that the good part isn't the big finish. If I grab this like a finish, I'll have learnt nothing.
* [sincere] "I was going to say the same. I always start things the way I leave them. Fast."
    @rel daniel trust+1
    you: I'd like to find out what I'm like slow.
    daniel[smile]: I've seen you slow. You looked at the floor before you pushed a chair. It was the most attractive thing that happened all night.
* [playful] "So we're agreed. We like each other, and we're going to be extremely unhurried about it."
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    daniel[laugh]: The least hurried on record. Songha will have to invent a new kind of schedule.
* [quiet] Nod. Move your hand along the wall until it's next to his.
    @rel daniel romance+1
    > Beside it. Not on it. The edges of your little fingers touching, like the bench. He looks down, and leaves it exactly there.
daniel[smile]: I do need one thing on a list, though. One. I'm still me.
you: Go on.
daniel: The first night it rains in July. The booth outside the arcade in Hongdae, under the useless awning. Nine o'clock.
daniel: Bring your half of the strip. I'll bring mine. We put them back together, and then we go in and take frame nine.
you: And if I want to say something before July?
daniel[laugh]: Then say it. It's not a lock, it's a booth. I'm seeing you next week anyway. I've decided that, if you'll have it.
daniel[neutral]: July's just so there's one night where we both know. Where neither of us has to wonder if it's a good moment.
you: What else do I bring?
daniel: Four thousand won. You still owe me for the first one.
you: Plus interest.
daniel[smile]: I'll waive the interest. I'm not waiving the four thousand. It's the principle.
> You take the pen out of your coat. It's still Songha's. You write it on the back of your half, under his arrow, where *FRAME NINE →* points off the edge of the paper.
> *First rain of July. 9. The awning. ₩4,000.*
@cg cg_daniel_x6
> He reads it over your arm, and then holds out his own half for you to write it there too, so that both copies say the same thing.
@if var.danielx_twelve == "blank"
    > On the folded page there's a twelve with two small words after it, in his writing: *a next one*. He takes the pen and, carefully, adds a date.
@sfx page
> Then the sun comes up. It just does it. Over the laundromat, with no help from anyone, one bright edge and then all of it.
daniel[smile]: Number ten.
> He gets the list out. He doesn't tick it. He gives you the page, and holds the pen with you, and the two of you make one slightly crooked tick together.
daniel[smile]: Done. Everything's closed. Songha's going to frame it.
@show songha neutral at=l
songha: I can hear you. I'm on the stairs. Breakfast is in nine minutes and I'm two people short.
daniel: Five more minutes.
@cg off
songha[smile]: …You have four.
@hide songha
> Four minutes. You spend them doing nothing, side by side at a low wall, with the light coming across the roof and warming one half of each of you.
> You're not leaving, and nothing is ending. There's a night in July with your name on it, and a week before that with a booth in it, and breakfast in four minutes.
> For the first time you can remember, there's somewhere you have to be later. Daniel hums. It sounds a little like rain.
@ending daniel_someday
@credits
